  ('davos-switzerland', '01F', 'Davos', 'Switzerland', 'Europe''s high-alpine all-rounder', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Switzerland & the Alps', '{"ski","culture","wellness","hiking","ultra"}', '{"alpine","refined","dramatic"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Highest town in the Alps at 1,560 m; former tuberculosis climate-cure resort (Thomas Mann''s Magic Mountain); population ~11,000-12,000","Davos Klosters Mountains: ~300 km slopes, 6 mountains (Parsenn, Jakobshorn, Madrisa, Rinerhorn, Schatzalp, Pischa), 57 transport systems","Parsenn: 95.5 km slopes, 810-2,844 m, 18 lifts; the 12 km Weissfluhgipfel-Kublis descent is one of Europe''s longest runs","Jakobshorn (freestyle): 41.2 km slopes, 1,535-2,568 m, Jatz Park; Klosters Gotschna cable car to 2,285 m + Madrisa to 2,602 m","Spengler Cup since 1923 (Dr Carl Spengler) — oldest club ice-hockey tournament in the world; 98th ed. 26-31 Dec 2026; HC Davos record 17 titles (2025)","World Economic Forum hosted every January since 1971 (2,500+ delegates); Davos leads the global mountain meeting market","Kirchner Museum (Gigon & Guyer, opened 1992, Daylight Award 2012) holds the world''s largest Ernst Ludwig Kirchner (1880-1938) collection","Cradle of ski tourism: world''s first T-bar drag-lift on the Bolgen 1934; home of the SLF national avalanche-research institute (since 1945); 8 toboggan runs; 700 km bike net + Alps Epic Trail Davos"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 117 police / 118 fire / 144 ambulance / 1414 REGA alpine air-rescue / 145 poison","hospital":"Spital Davos 24/7 emergency centre + rescue (emergency +41 81 414 88 88 / 144); trauma transfer Chur/Zurich, often by REGA","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-alpine winter sports: off-piste avalanche risk (SLF daily bulletin, 5-level scale; transceiver/shovel/probe + guide; the Wang/Gotschnagrat off-piste is lethal), altitude/AMS (town 1,560 m to Weissfluhgipfel 2,84